From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci: add Host Version 4 mode

U-Boot's SDHCI driver has no notion of Host Version 4 mode at all:
SDHCI_CTRL_V4_MODE does not exist, and SDHCI_SPEC_400 appears only as a
version constant. Linux has had it since 4.20 (sdhci_enable_v4_mode()),
and a controller that is driven in v4 mode by one driver and v3 mode by
another does not necessarily behave the same in both.

Cadence SD4HC on the Axera AX630C reports SDHCI_HOST_VERSION 0x0003,
which is spec 4.00, and Linux runs it with HOST_CONTROL2 = 0x3008 --
v4 mode and 64-bit addressing both on. U-Boot ran it in v3 mode.

Add the flag, let a host driver opt in before sdhci_probe(), and
re-apply the mode after the RESET_ALL in sdhci_init(), which clears
HOST_CONTROL2. Only the v4-mode bit is set: 64-bit addressing is a
separate bit that changes the descriptor width to the 128-bit v4 format,
which U-Boot's USE_ADMA64 path does not implement -- its descriptor is
the 96-bit v3 one.

The block count deliberately stays in the 16-bit register. The 32-bit
block count at SDHCI_32BIT_BLK_CNT is a 4.10 feature that Linux uses
only behind SDHCI_QUIRK2_USE_32BIT_BLK_CNT; on a 4.00 controller,
zeroing the 16-bit register gives every transfer a block count of zero
and identification fails at the first EXT_CSD read. Measured.

Signed-off-by: open-nanokvm-pro contributors <nanokvm@localhost>
---
 drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c |  1 +
 drivers/mmc/sdhci.c         | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 include/sdhci.h             |  6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/sdhci.h b/include/sdhci.h
--- a/include/sdhci.h
+++ b/include/sdhci.h
@@ -23,3 +23,5 @@
 #define SDHCI_DMA_ADDRESS	0x00
+/* Host Version 4 only: the 32-bit block count shares this address. */
+#define SDHCI_32BIT_BLK_CNT	0x00
 
 #define SDHCI_BLOCK_SIZE	0x04
diff --git a/include/sdhci.h b/include/sdhci.h
--- a/include/sdhci.h
+++ b/include/sdhci.h
@@ -168,2 +170,4 @@
 #define  SDHCI_CTRL_TUNED_CLK		0x0080
+#define  SDHCI_CTRL_V4_MODE		0x1000
+#define  SDHCI_CTRL_64BIT_ADDR		0x2000
 #define  SDHCI_CTRL_PRESET_VAL_ENABLE	0x8000
diff --git a/include/sdhci.h b/include/sdhci.h
--- a/include/sdhci.h
+++ b/include/sdhci.h
@@ -356,3 +360,5 @@
 	void *align_buffer;
 	bool force_align_buffer;
+	/* Host Version 4 mode: 32-bit block count. Set before sdhci_probe(). */
+	bool v4_mode;
 	dma_addr_t start_addr;
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
@@ -716,2 +721,19 @@
 
+/*
+ * Host Version 4 Enable. A RESET_ALL clears HOST_CONTROL2, so every caller
+ * that issues one has to put the mode back; the read-modify-write keeps the
+ * signal voltage and the UHS field the rest of the driver owns.
+ */
+static void sdhci_enable_v4_mode(struct sdhci_host *host)
+{
+	u16 ctrl2;
+
+	if (!host->v4_mode)
+		return;
+
+	ctrl2 = sdhci_readw(host, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL2);
+	ctrl2 |= SDHCI_CTRL_V4_MODE;
+	sdhci_writew(host, ctrl2, SDHCI_HOST_CONTROL2);
+}
+
 static int sdhci_init(struct mmc *mmc)
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
@@ -726,2 +748,3 @@
 	sdhci_reset(host, SDHCI_RESET_ALL);
+	sdhci_enable_v4_mode(host);
 
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci-cadence.c
@@ -269,2 +269,3 @@
 	host->quirks |= SDHCI_QUIRK_WAIT_SEND_CMD;
+	host->v4_mode = true;
 	sdhci_cdns_mmc_ops = sdhci_ops;
